{
  "slug": "planning-skills-for-agents-and-humans",
  "name": "Planning Skills For Agents And Humans",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Shaping (solution defining) skills so you, your team, and/or your AI agents can build with confidence and direction.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **13 skills** and **17 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (13): `breadboard-reflection` (Compare accepted intent with implementation reality when code or a prototype exists, preserve both separately, surface drift and…), `breadboarding` (Map current behavior, candidate shapes, or a selected design into places, affordances, stores, consequences, and wiring when concrete…), `dumplink` (Turn a selected, bounded project into sequenced vertical task groups with dependencies, risks, appetite-based cuts, acceptance checks, and…), `executable-breadboards` (Turn a selected slice into fixtures, example runs, expected outputs, edge cases, and acceptance tests when it is…), `feed-planning-context` (Prepare a compact context packet when an implementation agent needs the authoritative planning subset, execution contract, non-goals, and…), `framing-doc` (Create a frame from research, notes, requests, or transcripts when the current problem, desired outcome, boundaries, and evidence…), `interface-contracts` (Define plain-language inputs, outputs, branches, errors, and open decisions when a selected slice crosses a meaningful data, service,…), `kickoff-doc` (Create a builder-facing kickoff document from accepted planning artifacts when a team needs a durable reference organized by…), and 5 more\n- **Commands** (17): `appetite` (Set the bounded time or scope budget and cut line before selecting a solution shape), `breadboard` (Map current behavior, one candidate shape, or a selected design into places, affordances, stores, consequences, and wiring), `check-drift` (Check implementation direction against selected planning artifacts and stop if drift is found), `criteria` (Create or update only the requirements / criteria table before sketching solution shapes), `dumplink` (Turn a selected project into vertical task groups, dependency-aware sequence, risk states, cuts, and a bounded handoff), `feed-context` (Package planning artifacts into a compact context packet for implementation work), `fit-check` (Run fit checks and reverse fit checks across existing shapes without selecting a direction), `frame` (Create a framing document from notes, messages, transcripts, or source files), and 9 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install planning-skills-for-agents-and-humans@claude-community` from `mattlane66/planning-skills-for-agents-and-humans`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 13,
    "command": 17
  },
